<title>SINGAPORE: UOP aims to maintain 10-pct growth in 1997.</title>
<headline>UOP aims to maintain 10-pct growth in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>UOP, a partnership between Allied Signal Inc and Union Carbide Corp, is hoping to maintain its revenue growth of 10 percent in 1997, a senior company official said on Friday.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have been growing at better than 10 percent as a company...(we) want to keep that growth on track,&quot; Richard Wilmoth, UOP's managing director in Asia said at the opening of its Singapore office.</p>
<p>UOP, a supplier and licenser of technologies to oil and gas related industries saw 1996 revenues of over U.S.$1 billion.</p>
<p>The company said the Asia-Pacific region which contributes around half of its revenue will be the big growth area.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
</text>
